\caption(Explicit compact-model Adam fits, retaining every block. Training uses independent crop/flip augmentation and batch BN moments; inference validation selects paired parameter/moving-state checkpoints. Test subsets are used only after selection.)
\alttext(Explicit compact-model Adam fits, retaining every block. Training uses independent crop/flip augmentation and batch BN moments; inference validation selects paired parameter/moving-state checkpoints. Test subsets are used only after selection.)


The selected test-subset accuracies for depths 50/101/152 are 12.5%, 12.5%
and 6.25% (4, 4 and 2 of 32), with NLLs 2.527230, 3.969295 and 2.818557: after
only 20 updates each model is still near chance (NLL ln 10 ≈ 2.30), and these
short runs are not monotonic in depth. The training traces use batch moments and
augmentation; the selected training-NLL column instead evaluates unmodified fitting
images with saved inference moments, which have had few updates to settle. The two
quantities need not agree, and here the inference-mode training NLL is the larger.

> Native confusion matrices

These matrices use the held-out predictions from the executed program above.
The native `ConfusionMatrix` SVG API labels exact counts with true classes
running from top to bottom and predicted classes from left to right.

\image(figures/resnet_bottleneck_confusion_api_0.svg)
