\caption(Held-out classification confusion counts, evaluation 2. Exact cell counts are printed in the image.)
\alttext(Integer prediction counts with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)

\image(figures/resnet_bottleneck_confusion_api_2.svg)
\caption(Held-out classification confusion counts, evaluation 3. Exact cell counts are printed in the image.)
\alttext(Integer prediction counts with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)


> Conclusion

Bottlenecks trade a narrow learned spatial pathway for a wider residual representation.
Stride placement changes the evidence entering that pathway even with shared weights. Exact
sampling fixtures, complete-depth shape/count checks, finite gradients and explicit subset
fits test these separate claims without asserting benchmark performance or universal depth benefits.

